Article 65
(1) In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of KLA policy in the Region, a KLA Task Force shall be established.
(2) The establishment and membership composition of the KLA Task Force shall be determined by Regent's Decree.
(3) The Regent shall appoint the head of Bappeda as the KLA Task Force and the head of the OPD responsible for women's empowerment as secretary of the KLA Task Force;
(4) The KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), shall have the following main duties:
a. coordinating the implementation of policies and development of KLA; b. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on KLA policy;
c. collecting basic data for KLA development;
d. conducting needs analysis sourced from basic data; e. conducting dissemination of basic data;
f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing KLA, which are adjusted to regional potential;
g. preparing a 5 (five) year Child Friendly City regional action plan and work mechanism; and
h. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least once (1) a year.

