Article 9
The Regional Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter c has the following tasks:
a. promoting and facilitating Gender Mainstreaming to each OPD;
b. conducting socialization and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to Sub-district Heads and Wali Nagari;
c. preparing work programs every year;
d. encouraging the realization of Gender Responsive planning and budgeting;
e. preparing the work plan of the Gender Mainstreaming working group every year;
f. being responsible to the Regent through the Vice Regent;
g. formulating gender mainstreaming policy recommendations to the Regent;
h. preparing the Regional Gender profile;
i. monitoring the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in each OPD;
j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;
k. preparing a regional action plan on Gender Mainstreaming in the Region; and
l. encouraging the implementation of selection and appointment of focal points in each OPD.

Article 11
(1) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point in each OPD as referred to in Article 9 letter l consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or program duties.
(2) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the following duties:
a. promoting Gender Mainstreaming in the work unit;
b. facilitating the preparation of work plans and budgeting of OPD that are gender responsive;
c. implementing training, socialization, advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the OPD environment;
d. reporting the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming to the leadership of the OPD;
e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis on policies, programs, and activities in the work unit; and
f. facilitating the preparation of gender data in each OPD;
(3) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and determined by the leadership of the OPD.

Article 5
(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:
a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity and worth;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Region;
c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region;
d. enhancing Women's Empowerment in terms of role, quality and capacity in the fields of:
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social; and
4. economy.
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing Women's Empowerment services in the Region;
(2) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus Organizations in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 46
The regional disaggregated data working group as referred to in article 44 has the following duties:
a. to prepare a work plan for the gender and child disaggregated data working group using measurable indicators and targets for a specific period which will be used for monitoring and evaluation of the gender and child disaggregated data working group activities;
b. to enhance cross-sectoral cooperation in the framework of strengthening data produced related to the procurement and utilization of data;
c. to implement coordination and synchronization with relevant agencies in the framework of compiling gender and child data at the district level; and
d. to collect, process, compile and improve the quality of data as well as present data in regional apparatus organizations and subsequently use it as secondary data on Gender and Child data on an ongoing basis.

